body:
Tried to do it but rust doesn't like it: `ret` is a `Option<String>` but `Some("")` is a `Option<str>`. And `Some(String::from(""))` is an illegal function call in the match and matching `ret.ref()` doesn't work because ret is an Option  :-(

The best I could come up with is 

``` 
if ret.is_none() {
            return None
        } else {
            let s = ret.unwrap();
            match s.as_str() {
                "" => None,
                _ => Some(s),
            }
        }
``` 

and this doesn't look much better than what is in there now :-(

